# CAGED: One Chord, Five Shapes (repertoire plan: st-caged-chords). An original 20-bar study,
# one shape per bar. C climbs the neck in its five shapes: C (x32010), A shape at fret 3 (x35553),
# G shape (875558), E shape at fret 8 (8-10-10-9-8-8), D shape (x-x-10-12-13-12) and the C shape
# again twelve frets up (x-15-14-12-13-12); then back down to the open C. G climbs the same way:
# G (320003), E shape (355433), D shape (x-x-5-7-8-7), C shape (x-10-9-7-8-7), A shape
# (x-10-12-12-12-10), and back down to the open G.
# Every bar: the lowest root alone on beat 1, the whole shape on beat 2, the next root up alone on
# beat 3, the whole shape on beat 4. The finger on each root is the one the chord box shows.
title: CAGED: One Chord, Five Shapes
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the CAGED shapes of C and G
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
tags: caged, chord shapes, roots, whole neck
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
key: C

track: Your shapes
role: rhythm
